  "summary": {
    "as": "Reported to House",
    "asOf": "2026-10-09",
    "date": "2026-11-04T00:05:18Z",
    "text": "Disaster Loan Outreach Consistency Act\n\nThis bill requires the Small Business Administration (SBA) to ensure that\u00a0outreach materials for its disaster loan program (e.g., press releases, fact sheets) are accurate, current, and consistent across all\u00a0disaster field operations centers. (The SBA Disaster Loan Program provides low-interest loans to homeowners, renters, businesses, and nonprofits to assist with recovering from declared disasters.)\n\nSpecifically, the\u00a0SBA must (1) include in outreach materials updated information on the eligibility processes for and terms of the disaster loan program; (2) verify, prior to public release, that outreach materials are\u00a0current; and (3) annually review outreach materials to ensure consistency across disaster field operations centers.\u00a0"
  },
